{
 "esm": "0.8.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "latlon3d_transport_cwc_moving_lid",
  "description": "MOVING-LID consistency with continuity (CWC): free-stream preservation for the TERRAIN-FOLLOWING vertical transport stack while the level thicknesses BREATHE. The production counterpart of latlon3d_transport_cwc_3d_ppm, but on a hybrid sigma-pressure vertical coordinate whose layers move in time. Carries the AIR MASS m (the breathing pressure thickness) and the TRACER MASS mq, derives q = mq/m, and runs four rules: the zonal continuity + monotone-PPM pair (unchanged) and the NEW terrain-following vertical pair -- face_flux_divergence_lev_massform_noflux_bc (mass form, no /dz) for the air mass and ppm_flux_D_lev_mono_hybrid_noflux_bc (mass-form divergence + rank-3 breathing dp reconstruction widths) for the tracer.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS (the finding behind it). The fixed-grid vertical divergence divides by dz, so it is conservative ONLY when dz is constant in time; on a breathing grid it omits the grid-motion term and a uniform tracer drifts. This gate uses the mass-form divergence (the raw flux difference) so the air mass m is integrated as an extensive quantity, and DIAGNOSES the vertical air-mass flux Mz from continuity (Mz = -horiz*phi, phi vanishing at both walls) so that m stays equal to the hybrid dA[k]+dB[k]*Ps(i,j,t) as the surface pressure redistributes zonally. The layers genuinely move -- the reconstruction widths dp = m are three-dimensional and time-varying.\n\nTHE PROPERTY UNDER TEST. At q == 1 every CW84 slope is exactly 0.0, so the parabola is the constant 1 regardless of the breathing widths, the flux collapses to F = Mz bitwise, and the terrain-following PPM collapses onto the mass-form continuity -- so dmq/dt equals dm/dt to the last bit and dev = mq - m stays EXACTLY 0 while the grid moves. The reference is the CONSTANT ZERO, so non-vacuity is established by the companion falsifier (problems/_falsifier_moving_lid.esm, ic(mq) x 1.000001): with q != 1 the reconstruction is no longer flat, the tracer no longer tracks the breathing air mass, and dev drifts far above the 1e-12 tolerance. Only the t>0 assertion discriminates: dev is a state with dev(0)=0 by construction.\n\nMESH 12x7x9 (NLEV=9 >= 7 for the monotone lev rule; NLON=12 for the zonal wrap). The wind is a steady, cos(lat)-tapered zonal flux that drives a zonal surface-pressure redistribution; the air mass breathes over the span while staying positive.",
  "license": "MIT",
  "tags": [
   "esd:problem",
   "grid:latlon3d",
   "family:finite_volume",
   "op:D",
   "axes:lon,lat,lev",
   "scheme:flux_form",
   "property:free_stream"
  ]
 },
 "models": {
  "TransportCWCMovingLid": {
   "expression_template_imports": [
    {
     "ref": "../grids/latlon3d/rules/face_flux_divergence_lon_periodic.esm",
     "bindings": {
      "NLON": 12,
      "NLAT": 7,
      "NLEV": 9
     }
    },
    {
     "ref": "../grids/latlon3d/rules/face_flux_divergence_lev_massform_noflux_bc.esm",
     "bindings": {
      "NLON": 12,
      "NLAT": 7,
      "NLEV": 9
     }
    },
    {
     "ref": "../grids/latlon3d/rules/ppm_flux_D_lon_mono_periodic.esm",
     "bindings": {
      "NLON": 12,
      "NLAT": 7,
      "NLEV": 9
     }
    },
    {
     "ref": "../grids/latlon3d/rules/ppm_flux_D_lev_mono_hybrid_noflux_bc.esm",
     "bindings": {
      "NLON": 12,
      "NLAT": 7,
      "NLEV": 9
     }
    }
   ],
   "variables": {
    "lon0_deg": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "deg",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "Grid lon0_deg; 0 closes the periodic zonal circle."
    },
    "lat0_deg": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "deg",
     "default": -90.0,
     "description": "Grid lat0_deg; -90 pole-to-pole."
    },
    "dlon_deg": {
     "type": "observed",
     "units": "deg",
     "expression": {
      "op": "/",
      "args": [
       360.0,
       12
      ]
     },
     "description": "360/NLON=30 deg (literal; NLON consumed at the import edge, esm-spec 9.7.6)."
    },
    "dlat_deg": {
     "type": "observed",
     "units": "deg",
     "expression": {
      "op": "/",
      "args": [
       180.0,
       6
      ]
     },
     "description": "180/(NLAT-1)=30 deg; NLAT=7 floor for the monotone lat rule."
    },
    "phie": {
     "type": "observed",
     "units": "deg",
     "shape": [
      "lat_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "Latitude cell edges (grid lat_edge template); half-polar caps from the clamp.",
     "expression": {
      "op": "apply_expression_template",
      "args": [],
      "name": "lat_edge",
      "bindings": {}
     }
    },
    "coslat_e": {
     "type": "observed",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lat_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "cos of latitude edges; zero-length pole faces.",
     "expression": {
      "op": "apply_expression_template",
      "args": [],
      "name": "coslat_edge",
      "bindings": {
       "phie": "phie"
      }
     }
    },
    "dS_lat": {
     "type": "observed",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lat"
     ],
     "description": "Spherical cell-area weight sin(phie[j+1])-sin(phie[j]).",
     "expression": {
      "op": "apply_expression_template",
      "args": [],
      "name": "latcell_area",
      "bindings": {
       "phie": "phie"
      }
     }
    },
    "dphi_lat": {
     "type": "observed",
     "units": "rad",
     "shape": [
      "lat"
     ],
     "description": "Meridional cell extent (half-width at the caps).",
     "expression": {
      "op": "apply_expression_template",
      "args": [],
      "name": "latcell_dphi",
      "bindings": {
       "phie": "phie"
      }
     }
    },
    "m": {
     "type": "state",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lon",
      "lat",
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "AIR MASS per unit area in the cell (the breathing pressure thickness dp). Evolved by the mass-form continuity; stays equal to the hybrid dA[k]+dB[k]*Ps(i,j,t) because the vertical air-mass flux Mz is diagnosed from continuity."
    },
    "mq": {
     "type": "state",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lon",
      "lat",
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "TRACER MASS per unit area. Initialised bitwise equal to m so q=mq/m==1."
    },
    "dev": {
     "type": "state",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lon",
      "lat",
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Diagnostic deviation dev=mq-m, integrated from dev(0)=0 as (mq rhs)-(m rhs). At q==1 the terrain-following PPM collapses onto the mass-form continuity bitwise, so dev never leaves 0."
    },
    "dp": {
     "type": "observed",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lon",
      "lat",
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Reconstruction width for the terrain-following vertical PPM: an alias of the air-mass state m (the physical layer thickness). The rule's free name `dp` binds here.",
     "expression": {
      "op": "aggregate",
      "output_idx": [
       "i",
       "j",
       "k"
      ],
      "args": [
       "m"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "i": {
        "from": "lon"
       },
       "j": {
        "from": "lat"
       },
       "k": {
        "from": "lev"
       }
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "index",
       "args": [
        "m",
        "i",
        "j",
        "k"
       ]
      }
     }
    },
    "q": {
     "type": "observed",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lon",
      "lat",
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Mixing ratio mq/m; the quantity under test, must stay 1.",
     "expression": {
      "op": "aggregate",
      "output_idx": [
       "i",
       "j",
       "k"
      ],
      "args": [
       "mq",
       "m"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "i": {
        "from": "lon"
       },
       "j": {
        "from": "lat"
       },
       "k": {
        "from": "lev"
       }
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "/",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "index",
         "args": [
          "mq",
          "i",
          "j",
          "k"
         ]
        },
        {
         "op": "index",
         "args": [
          "m",
          "i",
          "j",
          "k"
         ]
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
    "Mx": {
     "type": "observed",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lon_nodes",
      "lat",
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Zonal face air-mass flux (west edge), vertically uniform, tapered by cos(lat) so the polar metric stays bounded. Steady in time; drives a zonal surface-pressure redistribution.",
     "expression": {
      "op": "aggregate",
      "output_idx": [
       "ci",
       "cj",
       "ck"
      ],
      "args": [],
      "ranges": {
       "ci": {
        "from": "lon_nodes"
       },
       "cj": {
        "from": "lat"
       },
       "ck": {
        "from": "lev"
       }
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "*",
       "args": [
        0.15,
        {
         "op": "sin",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "*",
           "args": [
            {
             "op": "*",
             "args": [
              {
               "op": "-",
               "args": [
                "ci",
                1
               ]
              },
              30.0
             ]
            },
            0.017453292519943295
           ]
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "op": "cos",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "*",
           "args": [
            {
             "op": "+",
             "args": [
              -90.0,
              {
               "op": "*",
               "args": [
                {
                 "op": "-",
                 "args": [
                  "cj",
                  1
                 ]
                },
                30.0
               ]
              }
             ]
            },
            0.017453292519943295
           ]
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
    "horiz": {
     "type": "observed",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lon",
      "lat",
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Zonal air-mass convergence D(Mx, wrt: lon); the same discrete operator the tracer PPM collapses to at q==1. Vertically uniform because Mx is.",
     "expression": {
      "op": "D",
      "args": [
       "Mx"
      ],
      "wrt": "lon"
     }
    },
    "Mz": {
     "type": "observed",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lon",
      "lat",
      "lev_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "Vertical air-mass flux DIAGNOSED from continuity: Mz[i,j,kn] = -horiz[i,j,1]*phi(kn), phi(kn)=(kn-1)-(kn-1)^2/NLEV vanishing at kn=1 (ground) and kn=NLEV+1 (top). This makes the mass-form continuity reproduce the hybrid tendency dB[k]*dPs/dt exactly, so m stays terrain-following-consistent.",
     "expression": {
      "op": "aggregate",
      "output_idx": [
       "ci",
       "cj",
       "ckn"
      ],
      "args": [
       "horiz"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "ci": {
        "from": "lon"
       },
       "cj": {
        "from": "lat"
       },
       "ckn": {
        "from": "lev_nodes"
       }
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "*",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "-",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "index",
           "args": [
            "horiz",
            "ci",
            "cj",
            1
           ]
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "op": "-",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "-",
           "args": [
            "ckn",
            1
           ]
          },
          {
           "op": "/",
           "args": [
            {
             "op": "*",
             "args": [
              {
               "op": "-",
               "args": [
                "ckn",
                1
               ]
              },
              {
               "op": "-",
               "args": [
                "ckn",
                1
               ]
              }
             ]
            },
            9.0
           ]
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    }
   },
